Well there is already the swamp level but most of the stuff there moves
pretty slow.
A few new level ideas would make Hell more interesting.
A regular maze level with walls to hard to dig and no teleport. This should
show up randomly and not often but at least once. This would make the run
more difficult.

A few levels like the plane of fire, which would combine the effects of the
big room with the lava.

Maybe a level that consists of spans between platforms. I don't know how
this should look as it would need a new tile. But basicly a level where if
you move off the platforms or bridge you fall.

The later two would be made pointless by levitation which only takes up a
ring slot. Other things you could do to make the end more interesting is let
Rodney summon demons. While they are not a real threat by themselves, I
would immagine that when your trying to get out they become less fun
considering there affinity for the up stairs.

If you want to be stereotypical you could put some sort of timer where you
have to get out by a certain time. Otherwise the dungeon collapses.

If you want to be truely evil you could have going up the stairs with the
amulet have a chance of generating a new level. Kind of like the mysterious
force, the place is activily working against you. Having to remap the level
would be painful at best and would use resources.



